msgid "AS BELOW SO ABOVE"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «AS BELOW SO ABOVE» (woh_nana:57).
msgctxt "woh_nana:58"
msgid "Coming not from above, but below, IKT-YOSIS has been resting in a gargantuan chamber underneath the mountains. A series of rituals has begun to reshape the world, weakening the walls of its tomb."
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «AS BELOW SO ABOVE» (woh_nana:57). Opciones: [new WEIRD WEATHER effects] · IKT-YOSIS.
msgctxt "woh_nana:59"
msgid "[new WEIRD WEATHER effects]"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «AS BELOW SO ABOVE» (woh_nana:57). Opciones: [new WEIRD WEATHER effects] · IKT-YOSIS.
msgctxt "woh_nana:60"
msgid "IKT-YOSIS"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «AS BELOW SO ABOVE» (woh_nana:57).
msgctxt "woh_nana:61"
msgid "The prophecy was right, and there was nothing you could do to stop it. KTU-RUFU’s dream of SHIOKAWA has ended."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «AS BELOW SO ABOVE» (woh_nana:57).
msgctxt "woh_nana:62"
msgid "Being a part of this dream, you and everyone you know have ceased to exist…"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «AS BELOW SO ABOVE» (woh_nana:57).
msgctxt "woh_nana:63"
msgid "Just a dream?..."
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:64"
msgid "RESHAPING SHIOKAWA"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «RESHAPING SHIOKAWA» (woh_nana:64).
msgctxt "woh_nana:65"
msgid "A second eldritch weather effect will activate each mystery."
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «RESHAPING SHIOKAWA» (woh_nana:64). Opciones: <<was it all just a dream?>> · SATOSHI MURAMATSU · HIKER.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:66"
msgid "<<was it all just a dream?>>"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «RESHAPING SHIOKAWA» (woh_nana:64). Opciones: <<was it all just a dream?>> · SATOSHI MURAMATSU · HIKER.
msgctxt "woh_nana:67"
msgid "SATOSHI MURAMATSU"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «RESHAPING SHIOKAWA» (woh_nana:64). Opciones: <<was it all just a dream?>> · SATOSHI MURAMATSU · HIKER.
msgctxt "woh_nana:68"
msgid "HIKER"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «RESHAPING SHIOKAWA» (woh_nana:64).
msgctxt "woh_nana:69"
msgid ""
"Name: SATOSHI MURAMATSU\n"
"23 / MALE\n"
" \n"
"Growing up in a small village, hiking wasn’t just a hobby for SATOSHI. It was a way to escape a home that always felt too small.\n"
"Recently, the once-familiar trails began changing and the landmarks disappearing, replaced by weird shrines."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «RESHAPING SHIOKAWA» (woh_nana:64).
msgctxt "woh_nana:70"
msgid ""
"+DEXTERITY\n"
"-PERCEPTION\n"
"starts with TRAIL WISDOM"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_nana:71"
msgid "SATOSHI"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:72"
msgid "BOTCHED BROADCAST"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «BOTCHED BROADCAST» (woh_nana:72).
msgctxt "woh_nana:73"
msgid ""
"While exploring the lesser-frequented mountain trails, you come across an abandoned mountain home. You decide to investigate it, finding an old TV.\n"
"\n"
"When you approach, it flickers to life, showing a broadcast of your face. It’s twisted, aged, and… screaming silently."
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «BOTCHED BROADCAST» (woh_nana:72). Opciones: smash the TV · watch silently · try to interact with the figure · ignore it and search the cabin.
msgctxt "woh_nana:74"
msgid "smash the TV"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «BOTCHED BROADCAST» (woh_nana:72). Opciones: smash the TV · watch silently · try to interact with the figure · ignore it and search the cabin.
msgctxt "woh_nana:75"
msgid "watch silently"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «BOTCHED BROADCAST» (woh_nana:72). Opciones: smash the TV · watch silently · try to interact with the figure · ignore it and search the cabin.
msgctxt "woh_nana:76"
msgid "try to interact with the figure"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «BOTCHED BROADCAST» (woh_nana:72). Opciones: smash the TV · watch silently · try to interact with the figure · ignore it and search the cabin.
msgctxt "woh_nana:77"
msgid "ignore it and search the cabin"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «BOTCHED BROADCAST» (woh_nana:72).
msgctxt "woh_nana:78"
msgid ""
"You pick up a broken chair leg and smash the TV. The eerie atmosphere ends in an instant, but you can’t help but shudder seeing the cables inside wriggle and pulse like tentacles or blood vessels.\n"
"You quickly exit the cabin, leaving the weird TV behind.\n"
"(+5 EXP / -1 REASON)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «BOTCHED BROADCAST» (woh_nana:72).
msgctxt "woh_nana:79"
msgid ""
"You stay still, stunned by the weird broadcast in front of you. You recognize some of your old injuries, now just faded scars on the figure's body on the TV. You also spot some new ones you don’t recognize. You make a mental note to protect these parts of your body.\n"
"(+10 EXP)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «BOTCHED BROADCAST» (woh_nana:72).
msgctxt "woh_nana:80"
msgid ""
"You stay still, stunned by the weird broadcast in front of you. But when the figure picks up a knife and moves it to the throat, you suddenly feel sick and avoid looking at it.\n"
"(-1 STAMINA)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «BOTCHED BROADCAST» (woh_nana:72).
msgctxt "woh_nana:81"
msgid ""
"You try to communicate with the older version of you, using your hands to gesture. To your surprise, the figure in the broadcast stops screaming and begins mimicking your stance and gestures. It feels strange, like looking into a mirror, but the knowledge that you’ll live long enough to get old is strangely comforting.\n"
"(+2 REASON)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «BOTCHED BROADCAST» (woh_nana:72).
msgctxt "woh_nana:82"
msgid ""
"You try to communicate with the older version of you, using your hands to gesture. The face in the broadcast ignores your attempts and you feel like you’re wasting your time.\n"
"(+2% DOOM)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «BOTCHED BROADCAST» (woh_nana:72).
msgctxt "woh_nana:83"
msgid ""
"You rummage through the cabin, trying to avoid the accusatory stare of your older self.\n"
"(+ITEM)"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:84"
msgid "HOT HOT SPRING"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «HOT HOT SPRING» (woh_nana:84).
msgctxt "woh_nana:85"
msgid "The overgrown hot spring steams invitingly, chasing away the chill. You almost want to ignore the bones floating in the water, clean and polished. The air smells of copper but it also reminds you of your best memories from childhood."
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «HOT HOT SPRING» (woh_nana:84). Opciones: enter the water · remove a bone for inspection · leave immediately.
msgctxt "woh_nana:86"
msgid "enter the water"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «HOT HOT SPRING» (woh_nana:84). Opciones: enter the water · remove a bone for inspection · leave immediately.
msgctxt "woh_nana:87"
msgid "remove a bone for inspection"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «HOT HOT SPRING» (woh_nana:84). Opciones: enter the water · remove a bone for inspection · leave immediately.
msgctxt "woh_nana:88"
msgid "leave immediately"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «HOT HOT SPRING» (woh_nana:84).
msgctxt "woh_nana:89"
msgid ""
"You remove your clothes, too eager to jump into the inviting spring. You soak in the weird coppery-smelling water feeling stronger and rejuvenated.\n"
"(+2 STAMINA)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «HOT HOT SPRING» (woh_nana:84).
msgctxt "woh_nana:90"
msgid ""
"You remove your clothes, too eager to jump into the inviting spring. You soak in the weird coppery-smelling water, totally oblivious to the searing heat slowly boiling you alive.\n"
"(-1 STAMINA / +INJURY)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «HOT HOT SPRING» (woh_nana:84).
msgctxt "woh_nana:91"
msgid ""
"You manage to fish out a bone, it looks like a human femur but you can’t be sure. It reminds you of the chicken bones stripped of meat after boiling the soup for too long.\n"
"(+5 EXPERIENCE)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «HOT HOT SPRING» (woh_nana:84).
msgctxt "woh_nana:92"
msgid ""
"You try to fish out the bone but burn your hands in the hot water.\n"
"(+INJURY)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «HOT HOT SPRING» (woh_nana:84).
msgctxt "woh_nana:93"
msgid ""
"You quickly leave the hot spring, not trusting yourself to stay near the hot spring any longer. You’re worried that you’ll think of the inviting water for days to come.\n"
"(-1 REASON)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «HOT HOT SPRING» (woh_nana:84).
msgctxt "woh_nana:94"
msgid "Required DOOM for the next card:"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «HOT HOT SPRING» (woh_nana:84).
msgctxt "woh_nana:95"
msgid "Pay 20 EXP to reveal another card."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «HOT HOT SPRING» (woh_nana:84).
msgctxt "woh_nana:96"
msgid "Pay 2 REASON to reveal another card."
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:97"
msgid "FOOD WASTE"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «FOOD WASTE» (woh_nana:97).
msgctxt "woh_nana:98"
msgid "One of the patrons is actively rotting where they sit, hunched over their bowl. They lift their head to order another, and collapse across the counter."
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «FOOD WASTE» (woh_nana:97). Opciones: keep watching.
msgctxt "woh_nana:99"
msgid "keep watching"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «FOOD WASTE» (woh_nana:97).
msgctxt "woh_nana:100"
msgid ""
"The staff wordlessly drag the patron's body into the kitchen...\n"
"(+3 EXPERIENCE / -2 REASON)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «FOOD WASTE» (woh_nana:97).
msgctxt "woh_nana:101"
msgid "share your SMELLY MEAT"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «FOOD WASTE» (woh_nana:97).
msgctxt "woh_nana:102"
msgid "[needs 'SMELLY MEAT' item]"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «FOOD WASTE» (woh_nana:97).
msgctxt "woh_nana:103"
msgid ""
"You share some of your SMELLY MEAT and manage to move forward without problems.\n"
"(-2% DOOM)"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:104"
msgid "INSATIABLE"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «INSATIABLE» (woh_nana:104).
msgctxt "woh_nana:105"
msgid "You're pretty sure that glassy-eyed patron in the corner was here yesterday, too. In that exact same spot, with the exact same ramen. You watch her for quite a while, but her bowl never runs empty, and she never stops eating, constantly pushing more into her lips..."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «INSATIABLE» (woh_nana:104).
msgctxt "woh_nana:106"
msgid ""
"As the woman eats, one of her fingers slips down her chopsticks and into her mouth.\n"
"She bites it clean off and swallows it down like the rest. And she just keeps eating.\n"
"\n"
"You're going to be sick.\n"
"(-2 STAMINA)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_nana:107"
msgid "RANCID QUEUE"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:108"
msgid "FREE SAMPLE"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «FREE SAMPLE» (woh_nana:108).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:109"
msgid ""
"<<Hey!!>> one of the patrons cries, suddenly thrusting herself upon you. She grabs your collar.\n"
"<<You've been waiting sooo long, right? Here! I'll give you some of mine!!>>\n"
"\n"
"She shoves a putrid ramen bowl into your face, expectantly watching with dull, twitching eyes..."
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «FREE SAMPLE» (woh_nana:108). Opciones: shove her away.
msgctxt "woh_nana:110"
msgid "shove her away"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «FREE SAMPLE» (woh_nana:108).
msgctxt "woh_nana:111"
msgid ""
"The girl slams into the pavement, the ramen spilling out of its bowl. She sits there, stunned, staring at you, not understanding what just happened. Then she screeches, suddenly rising to her feet and smashing the empty bowl over your head! You're left staggered and reeling as she storms off.\n"
"(+INJURY)"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:112"
msgid "PRACTICE MAKES PERFECT"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «PRACTICE MAKES PERFECT» (woh_nana:112).
msgctxt "woh_nana:113"
msgid "The smell of blood and decay overcomes you as you push open the door to the old maintenance room. Bodies upon bodies are piled here, all sewn together with the mismatched body parts of fish."
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «PRACTICE MAKES PERFECT» (woh_nana:112). Opciones: search through the bodies · examine the shelves.
msgctxt "woh_nana:114"
msgid "search through the bodies"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «PRACTICE MAKES PERFECT» (woh_nana:112). Opciones: search through the bodies · examine the shelves.
msgctxt "woh_nana:115"
msgid "examine the shelves"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «PRACTICE MAKES PERFECT» (woh_nana:112).
msgctxt "woh_nana:116"
msgid ""
"Your stomach ties itself in knots, but you hold it together. Your efforts are rewarded as you discover student ID cards from each of the corpses. These could be useful.\n"
"(+10 EXPERIENCE)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «PRACTICE MAKES PERFECT» (woh_nana:112).
msgctxt "woh_nana:117"
msgid ""
"You steel yourself as best you can, but soon lose your nerve, staggering out of the room and struggling not to vomit.\n"
"(-2 STAMINA)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «PRACTICE MAKES PERFECT» (woh_nana:112).
msgctxt "woh_nana:118"
msgid ""
"Among the various pieces of rusted equipment, you discover one of the bloodied tools the killer must have used for their twisted experiment.\n"
"(+ITEM)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «PRACTICE MAKES PERFECT» (woh_nana:112).
msgctxt "woh_nana:119"
msgid ""
"There's nothing of importance among the shelves. As you leave, the stench of death sticks to your clothes, a grim reminder of just how many you've already failed to save...\n"
"(+2% DOOM)"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:120"
msgid "SCALED TOME"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «SCALED TOME» (woh_nana:120).
msgctxt "woh_nana:121"
msgid ""
"In a dusty corner of the school library, one of the books sits alone on its shelf. Its appearance is slimy and damp, bound in what looks like fish scales.\n"
"\n"
"Something draws you toward it..."
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «SCALED TOME» (woh_nana:120). Opciones: read it.
msgctxt "woh_nana:122"
msgid "read it"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «SCALED TOME» (woh_nana:120).
msgctxt "woh_nana:123"
msgid "All the pages are written in a language you can't understand."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «SCALED TOME» (woh_nana:120).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:124"
msgid ""
">>... and so They wept onto the bare rock, and it grew rich with miserable life, purged from its home in the sea. But so long as their flesh craves water, and their souls unity, all mankind shall return to the waves.<<\n"
"\n"
"... maybe there's... something to this...\n"
"(-2 REASON / +CURSE)"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:125"
msgid "SOMETHING INSIDE"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «SOMETHING INSIDE» (woh_nana:125).
msgctxt "woh_nana:126"
msgid ""
"While moving through the hallway, a loud thud startles you. It came from the wall right next to you, so you start to think it must be from a room behind there...\n"
"...but isn't this wall on the outside of the building?\n"
"(-1 REASON / +5 EXPERIENCE)"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «SOMETHING INSIDE» (woh_nana:125). Opciones: BREAKING AND ENTERING.
msgctxt "woh_nana:127"
msgid "BREAKING AND ENTERING"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «SOMETHING INSIDE» (woh_nana:125).
msgctxt "woh_nana:128"
msgid "The entrance to the victim's apartment is locked and wrapped in caution tape. The place could hold valuable clues, but getting in without drawing any attention could be difficult…"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «SOMETHING INSIDE» (woh_nana:125).
msgctxt "woh_nana:129"
msgid "force it open"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «SOMETHING INSIDE» (woh_nana:125).
msgctxt "woh_nana:130"
msgid "pick the lock"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «SOMETHING INSIDE» (woh_nana:125).
msgctxt "woh_nana:131"
msgid ""
"You charge, slamming your shoulder against the door and throwing it wide open. Before anyone can notice you, you quickly inspect the place. The one detail that stands out to you is strange scuff marks around the vents...\n"
"(+5 EXPERIENCE)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «SOMETHING INSIDE» (woh_nana:125).
msgctxt "woh_nana:132"
msgid ""
"You throw your weight against the door several times, but it refuses to budge. All you get for your trouble are bruises the next morning.\n"
"(-1 STAMINA)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «SOMETHING INSIDE» (woh_nana:125).
msgctxt "woh_nana:133"
msgid ""
"The lock pops open with a click, and you slip into the apartment unnoticed. Upon investigating, it seems the victim was a model. You find a few strange letters on her desk from a 'distant admirer'. The contents are sickening.\n"
"(+7 EXPERIENCE)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «SOMETHING INSIDE» (woh_nana:125).
msgctxt "woh_nana:134"
msgid ""
"You concentrate, prodding a bobby pin around inside the lock, but it seems stuck. You hear a neighbor coming down the hallway and have to flee.\n"
"(+2% DOOM)"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:135"
msgid "AROUND IN CIRCLES"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «AROUND IN CIRCLES» (woh_nana:135).
msgctxt "woh_nana:136"
msgid ""
"You're hopelessly lost. All of these trees look exactly the same. You take a moment to stop, and try to get your bearings by thinking about where you've been...\n"
"\n"
"...only to find you can't remember anymore.\n"
"(-10 EXPERIENCE)"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «AROUND IN CIRCLES» (woh_nana:135). Opciones: MAW ALTAR.
msgctxt "woh_nana:137"
msgid "MAW ALTAR"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «AROUND IN CIRCLES» (woh_nana:135).
msgctxt "woh_nana:138"
msgid "In a clearing, you find a primitive altar, a symbol laid out with branches, enclosed in a ring of teeth. Teeth too large, too bent, too wrong to belong to anything natural."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «AROUND IN CIRCLES» (woh_nana:135).
msgctxt "woh_nana:139"
msgid "inspect the teeth"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «AROUND IN CIRCLES» (woh_nana:135).
msgctxt "woh_nana:140"
msgid "ignore the altar"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «AROUND IN CIRCLES» (woh_nana:135).
msgctxt "woh_nana:141"
msgid ""
"You pluck some of the teeth from the dirt and discover strange runes on the underside. It dawns on you that these might have been human teeth after all...\n"
"(+SPELL)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «AROUND IN CIRCLES» (woh_nana:135).
msgctxt "woh_nana:142"
msgid ""
"As you reach into the circle, you hear a sickening snap, and suddenly the teeth have closed up on you from the dirt like a bear trap! Screaming, you barely manage to free yourself without losing a limb to the jaws.\n"
"(+INJURY)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «AROUND IN CIRCLES» (woh_nana:135).
msgctxt "woh_nana:143"
msgid ""
"Although disconcerted by the sight, you keep heading along the way. You're barely a few meters away, though, when you hear an animal's cry and a disgusting crunch behind you.\n"
"\n"
"When you turn to look, the altar is gone. In its place is disturbed dirt and a decapitated deer's head, freshly bleeding from the neck.\n"
"(-3 REASON)"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:144"
msgid "VICTIM LEDGERS"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «VICTIM LEDGERS» (woh_nana:144).
msgctxt "woh_nana:145"
msgid ""
"You stumble onto a rusted-out shed. It doesn't look like it's been touched in years, but as you step inside, you find dozens of scrawled notes nailed to the walls.\n"
"\n"
"The most recent of these notes bears the names of the three missing students."
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «VICTIM LEDGERS» (woh_nana:144). Opciones: MAKOTO · JUNPEI · HITOMI.
msgctxt "woh_nana:146"
msgid "MAKOTO"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «VICTIM LEDGERS» (woh_nana:144). Opciones: MAKOTO · JUNPEI · HITOMI.
msgctxt "woh_nana:147"
msgid "JUNPEI"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «VICTIM LEDGERS» (woh_nana:144). Opciones: MAKOTO · JUNPEI · HITOMI.
msgctxt "woh_nana:148"
msgid "HITOMI"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «VICTIM LEDGERS» (woh_nana:144).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:149"
msgid ">>Combative. Left to wander. Succumbed to the woods. Sense of self was consumed. Followed obediently once retrieved. Nothing but a husk.<<"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «VICTIM LEDGERS» (woh_nana:144).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:150"
msgid ""
"\n"
"\n"
">>Offered unto the house.<<\n"
"(+5 EXPERIENCE)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «VICTIM LEDGERS» (woh_nana:144).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:151"
msgid ">>Emotional. Cried and pleaded. Lost all hope once isolated from his friends. Taken to the porch and harvested.<<"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «VICTIM LEDGERS» (woh_nana:144).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:152"
msgid ""
">>Desperate. Begged pathetically with every breath she could. Chosen to witness.<<\n"
">>Not a single word after that.<<"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_nana:153"
msgid "SUSPICIOUS APARTMENT"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_nana:154"
msgid "ICE AXE"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_nana:155"
msgid "+2 STR for the event skill checks"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_nana:156"
msgid "How did it end up in SHIOKAWA?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_nana:157"
msgid "useful and dangerous"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:158"
msgid "LUCKY COIN"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «LUCKY COIN» (woh_nana:158).
msgctxt "woh_nana:159"
msgid ""
"+1 LUCK\n"
"(use): succeed the next event stat check, breaks the item"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «LUCKY COIN» (woh_nana:158).
msgctxt "woh_nana:160"
msgid "How did this coin end up here?..."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «LUCKY COIN» (woh_nana:158).
msgctxt "woh_nana:161"
msgid "a medieval coin"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
