#. Parte de «SAFETY IN NUMBERS» (woh_perk:310).
msgctxt "woh_perk:313"
msgid "Chaos rises! All STATS improved!"
msgstr "¡El caos aumenta! ¡Mejoran todos los atributos!"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
#. Parte de «SAFETY IN NUMBERS» (woh_perk:310).
msgctxt "woh_perk:314"
msgid ""
"THE OLD GOD STIRS...\n"
"(click here to reveal its effect)"
msgstr ""
"EL DIOS ANTIGUO SE AGITA…\n"
"(clic aquí para revelar su efecto)"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:315"
msgid "「STORE CLOSED」"
msgstr "「TIENDA CERRADA」"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:316"
msgid "The [SHOP] additional action is disabled."
msgstr "La acción adicional [TIENDA] está deshabilitada"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:317"
msgid "The friendly dog disappeared last night. You will have to find a new place to buy equipment..."
msgstr "El perro amistoso desapareció durante la noche. Tendrás que buscar otro lugar para comprar equipamiento…"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:318"
msgid "「ROADS CLOSED」"
msgstr "「CAMINOS CERRADOS」"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:319"
msgid "Investigating places located outside the city (VILLAGE, MANSION, FOREST) costs 1% more DOOM."
msgstr "Investigar lugares fuera de la ciudad (ALDEA, MANSIÓN, BOSQUE) cuesta 1 % más de RUINA."

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:320"
msgid "Roads leading out of town were closed by the police. You'll have to find a new way out..."
msgstr "La policía cerró los caminos que salen de la ciudad. Tendrás que buscar otra forma de salir…"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:321"
msgid "「SCHOOL BURNED DOWN」"
msgstr "「ESCUELA QUEMADA」"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:322"
msgid "While classes will continue in an old wing, no student will gather in the schoolyard."
msgstr "Si bien las clases continuarán en un ala antigua, ningún estudiante puede ir al patio."

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:323"
msgid "While classes will continue in an old wing, no student will gather in the schoolyard."
msgstr "Si bien las clases continuarán en un ala antigua, ningún estudiante puede ir al patio."

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:324"
msgid "「RIOTS」"
msgstr "「ALBOROTOS」"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:325"
msgid "Dangerous bands of rioters gather around the DOWNTOWN area."
msgstr "Peligrosas pandillas de alborotadores se reúnen en el área del CENTRO DE LA CIUDAD"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:326"
msgid "Dangerous bands of rioters are gathering around the downtown area. The police are hopeless..."
msgstr "Peligrosas pandillas de alborotadores se reúnen en el área del centro de la ciudad. La policía no puede hacer nada…"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:327"
msgid "「WINDS OF PLAGUE」"
msgstr "「AIRES DE PLAGA」"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:328"
msgid "TREATMENT and SURGERY actions cost more"
msgstr "TRATAMIENTO y CIRUGÍA valen más"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:329"
msgid "A weird epidemic keeps staff at the hospital busy. Skipping the line will cost you more..."
msgstr "Una extraña epidemia tiene ocupado al personal del hospital. Saltarte la fila hará que te cobren más…"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:330"
msgid "「CUT OFF FROM THE OUTSIDE WORLD」"
msgstr "「DESCONECTADA DEL MUNDO」"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:331"
msgid "The whole town stopped receiving any outside signal. It must be the radio mast failure..."
msgstr "La ciudad dejó recibir señales del exterior. La torre de radio debe estar fallando…"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:332"
msgid "The whole town stopped receiving any outside signal. It must be the radio mast failure..."
msgstr "La ciudad dejó recibir señales del exterior. La torre de radio debe estar fallando…"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:333"
msgid "「FETID FUMES」"
msgstr "「GASES FÉTIDOS」"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:334"
msgid "Your REST action is less effective."
msgstr "DESCANSAR es menos efectivo."

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:335"
msgid "The air feels heavy, making it hard to breathe..."
msgstr "El aire se siente pesado, es difícil respirar…"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:336"
msgid "「CONTAMINATED WATER」"
msgstr "「AGUA CONTAMINADA」"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:337"
msgid "You can't regain health in between mysteries."
msgstr "No puedes recuperar salud entre misterios."

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:338"
msgid "There's something wrong with the tap water. It is black and oily and glistening, smelling like death. You hope it's just a temporary issue..."
msgstr "Algo extraño tiene el agua de grifo. Está negra, aceitosa y brillante, apesta a muerte. Esperas que solo sea temporal…"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:339"
msgid "「ARCANE STORM」"
msgstr "「TORMENTA ARCANA」"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:340"
msgid "REASON cost of all SPELLS is increased by 1."
msgstr "Aumenta en 1 el coste de CORDURA para todos los hechizos"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:341"
msgid "Local scientists are baffled. An unprecedented aurora-like event has bathed the entire town in an unnatural green glow..."
msgstr "Los científicos locales están impactados. Un evento sin precedentes similar a una aurora tiene a la ciudad resplandeciendo con un brillo de un verde poco natural…"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:342"
msgid "「PRICE HIKE」"
msgstr "「AUMENTO DE PRECIOS」"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:343"
msgid "All shop ITEMS cost 1 FUNDS more."
msgstr "Todos los objetos en la tienda valen 1 más de SALDO"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:344"
msgid "Preparing for the worst, people are stocking up on everything, making it harder for you to find what you want."
msgstr "Prepárate para lo peor, la gente está acaparando todo y te cuesta encontrar lo que quieres."

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:345"
msgid "「FREAKY FLOOD」"
msgstr "「INUNDACIÓN EXTRAÑA」"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:346"
msgid "Exploring the SEASIDE location has a chance of inflicting DRENCHED status."
msgstr "Explorar la COSTA tiene una probabilidad de infligir el estado MOJADO"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:347"
msgid "Did the water level suddenly increase or is our city slowly sinking?"
msgstr "¿El nivel del mar aumentó de la nada o la ciudad se está hundiendo lentamente?"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:348"
msgid "「HEART OF DARKNESS」"
msgstr "「CORAZÓN DE TINIEBLAS」"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:349"
msgid "Lighthouse gets one additional floor."
msgstr "El faro obtiene un piso extra."

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:350"
msgid "The imposing shadow cast by the old lighthouse is getting longer each day..."
msgstr "La imponente sombra del antiguo faro crece cada día que pasa…"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:351"
msgid "「SCHOOL CURFEW」"
msgstr "「TOQUE DE QUEDA ESCOLAR」"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:352"
msgid "The [LIBRARY] additional action is disabled."
msgstr "La acción adicional [BIBLIOTECA] está deshabilitada"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:353"
msgid "With more and more students going missing, the police have restricted access to the school's building."
msgstr "La policía restringió el acceso a las inmediaciones de la escuela debido a las constantes desapariciones de estudiantes."

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:354"
msgid "「TIME SKIP」"
msgstr "「SALTO TEMPORAL」"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:355"
msgid "+5% DOOM"
msgstr "+5 % de RUINA"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:356"
msgid "What? I'd have sworn it was Monday, not Tuesday... right?"
msgstr "¿Qué? Habría jurado que hoy era lunes, no martes…"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:357"
msgid "「BLOOD MOON」"
msgstr "「LUNA SANGRIENTA」"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:358"
msgid "All enemies get additional 20 POWER."
msgstr "Todos los enemigos obtienen 20 de PODER adicional"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:359"
msgid "The crimson moon spotted over SHIOKAWA keeps everyone on the edge..."
msgstr "La luna carmesí que se cierne sobre SHIOKAWA tiene a todos tensos…"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:360"
msgid "The flooded areas make it harder to navigate. (+ STATUS)"
msgstr "Es complicado navegar en las áreas inundadas. (+ESTADO)"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:361"
msgid "The ocean is calling you..."
msgstr "El océano te llama…"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:362"
msgid "You must enter the water. (-1 REASON)"
msgstr "Debes entrar al agua. (-1 de CORDURA)"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:363"
msgid "The underwater city is rising. (+1% DOOM)"
msgstr "La ciudad submarina se alza. (+1 % de RUINA)"

#. Mejoras (perks): nombre, efecto y mensaje al activarse.
msgctxt "woh_perk:364"
msgid "You continue to change. (-1 STAMINA)"
msgstr "Sigues cambiando. (-1 de VIGOR)"

#. Diálogo de JUNPEI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:0"
msgid "<<Sorry about all this,>> JUNPEI says again."
msgstr ""

#. Diálogo de HITOMI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:1"
msgid "<<At least it's nice not to be stuck at home,>> HITOMI sighs, trudging on."
msgstr ""

#. Diálogo de JUNPEI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:2"
msgid "JUNPEI frowns at his notes. <<Is this different from last time I was here?>>"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_roku:3"
msgid "HITOMI hums something slightly out of tune."
msgstr ""

#. Diálogo de JUNPEI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:4"
msgid "<<Dad's gonna kill me for being out this late again,>> JUNPEI thinks aloud."
msgstr ""

#. Diálogo de HITOMI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:5"
msgid "HITOMI kicks a rock down the path. <<Is filmmaking always this dull?>>"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_roku:6"
msgid "You fill the silence by chatting to JUNPEI about cinematography. It helps."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_roku:7"
msgid "It's going to take a while to get the mud off your clothes."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_roku:8"
msgid "Maybe you should've worn something more practical."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_roku:9"
msgid "You haven't heard any road noise for a while at this point."
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:10"
msgid "MASON CAIRN"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «MASON CAIRN» (woh_roku:10).
msgctxt "woh_roku:11"
msgid ""
"Jutting out of the grass stands a stack of weathered bricks. They're misshapen, haphazardly piled up at odd angles, but somehow the tower is stable.\n"
"\n"
"It looks like a monument to something, but it's hard to say what."
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «MASON CAIRN» (woh_roku:10). Opciones: look closely · topple it · ask JUNPEI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:12"
msgid "look closely"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «MASON CAIRN» (woh_roku:10). Opciones: look closely · topple it · ask JUNPEI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:13"
msgid "topple it"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «MASON CAIRN» (woh_roku:10). Opciones: look closely · topple it · ask JUNPEI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:14"
msgid "ask JUNPEI"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «MASON CAIRN» (woh_roku:10).
msgctxt "woh_roku:15"
msgid ""
"The dim light catches just right to reveal jagged etchings along the cairn's exterior. You realize each brick marks an entry in an ongoing history. But whose history - and what is it?\n"
"(+1 KNOWLEDGE / +15 EXPERIENCE)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «MASON CAIRN» (woh_roku:10).
msgctxt "woh_roku:16"
msgid ""
"It's all just bricks. You can't make anything more meaningful out of it than that. You're all the more agitated, wondering about the ominous structure.\n"
"(-1 REASON)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «MASON CAIRN» (woh_roku:10).
msgctxt "woh_roku:17"
msgid ""
"Driven by the unnerving presence of the tower, you shove it and collapse the entire thing. You regret it immediately. The dread hanging over you doubles - what, exactly, did you just spite?\n"
"(+ITEM / +STATUS / +CURSE)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «MASON CAIRN» (woh_roku:10).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:18"
msgid ""
"<<Huh? Oh, that... I guess someone made a cairn out of bricks. Cairns used to indicate graves, but nowadays they're usually trail markers.>>\n"
"\n"
"You're relieved it isn't supernatural, but now you're left wondering what it's leading you toward.\n"
"(+20 EXPERIENCE)"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:19"
msgid "REST YOUR HEAD"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «REST YOUR HEAD» (woh_roku:19).
msgctxt "woh_roku:20"
msgid "Propped up on a bed of rocks, a deep blue sofa comes into view before you. Moss climbs up the worn legs and back, but the arms and cushions are bizarrely clean and soft."
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «REST YOUR HEAD» (woh_roku:19). Opciones: ignore it · rest · relax with HITOMI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:21"
msgid "ignore it"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «REST YOUR HEAD» (woh_roku:19). Opciones: ignore it · rest · relax with HITOMI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:22"
msgid "rest"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «REST YOUR HEAD» (woh_roku:19). Opciones: ignore it · rest · relax with HITOMI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:23"
msgid "relax with HITOMI"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «REST YOUR HEAD» (woh_roku:19).
msgctxt "woh_roku:24"
msgid ""
"Despite the temptation to give up, you push on a little more than you thought you could.\n"
"(+1 STRENGTH)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «REST YOUR HEAD» (woh_roku:19).
msgctxt "woh_roku:25"
msgid ""
"You pretend you didn't see it and move on. But it's a reminder of how much this walking makes you ache.\n"
"(-2 STAMINA)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «REST YOUR HEAD» (woh_roku:19).
msgctxt "woh_roku:26"
msgid ""
"Sleep takes you the moment you let your head fall. Something rushes past your unconscious mind. Whispers, hands, repressed memories, unwanted premonitions. \n"
"\n"
"The fact that you don't remember a thing when you wake up doesn't worry you. What worries you is that you might remember later.\n"
"(+CURSE / +1 STAMINA)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «REST YOUR HEAD» (woh_roku:19).
msgctxt "woh_roku:27"
msgid ""
"Abruptly, HITOMI launches herself onto the sofa with a crash, nearly rolling it over in the process.\n"
"\n"
"You can tell she's really trying to inject some levity into the situation, but despite yourself, you can't help laughing as she kicks her legs up.\n"
"You sit with her for a while and breathe.\n"
"(+3 STAMINA / +3 REASON)"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:28"
msgid "TRACKS"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «TRACKS» (woh_roku:28).
msgctxt "woh_roku:29"
msgid "A set of bare footprints in the dirt catches your attention out of the monotony of the woods. But as you follow them, hoping for a lead, they just... stop. Right in the middle of a clearing."
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «TRACKS» (woh_roku:28). Opciones: investigate · look up.
msgctxt "woh_roku:30"
msgid "investigate"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «TRACKS» (woh_roku:28). Opciones: investigate · look up.
msgctxt "woh_roku:31"
msgid "look up"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «TRACKS» (woh_roku:28).
msgctxt "woh_roku:32"
msgid ""
"As you're searching for an explanation, you spot some carvings you recognize from JUNPEI's notes. Following them along the trees, you find a dirty coin hidden in a hollow. But all your questions remain unanswered.\n"
"(+ITEM)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «TRACKS» (woh_roku:28).
msgctxt "woh_roku:33"
msgid ""
"There is no explanation for any of this. You're left with no choice but to press on and try to forget about it. Easier said than done...\n"
"(-3 REASON)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «TRACKS» (woh_roku:28).
msgctxt "woh_roku:34"
msgid ""
"You lift the beam of your flashlight. It fades into the dark, but at the edge, past the leaves, you glimpse a narrow form, swaying, curling inward-\n"
"\n"
"Something primal strikes you. It doesn't matter what's up there. You turn off the flashlight and run until you can't breathe.\n"
"(+STATUS)"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:35"
msgid "TO NOWHERE"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «TO NOWHERE» (woh_roku:35).
msgctxt "woh_roku:36"
msgid "A set of ramshackle wooden stairs rises from the moss and into the foliage above. They aren't attached to anything, not even a tree. There's no reason for these to be built here. Something about that draws you in."
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «TO NOWHERE» (woh_roku:35). Opciones: climb.
msgctxt "woh_roku:37"
msgid "climb"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «TO NOWHERE» (woh_roku:35).
msgctxt "woh_roku:38"
msgid ""
"You take a few steps up, only to immediately fall through some rotten boards. Somehow, you manage to land safely. Maybe you're just a little more alert tonight.\n"
"(+1 DEXTERITY)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «TO NOWHERE» (woh_roku:35).
msgctxt "woh_roku:39"
msgid ""
"You climb the steps, leaves dragging along your skin as you scale upward, denser and darker - only to find that you're at the bottom of the stairs again. Like nothing happened at all.\n"
"(-2 REASON)"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:40"
msgid "TWIN TREES"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «TWIN TREES» (woh_roku:40).
msgctxt "woh_roku:41"
msgid ""
"Two trees grow tangled into one another, melding into a single trunk that vanishes into the canopy, a natural archway.\n"
"\n"
"You look through the gap in the twin trees. Then you look from the side. Somehow, the arrangement of the trees is different."
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «TWIN TREES» (woh_roku:40). Opciones: pass through · go around.
msgctxt "woh_roku:42"
msgid "pass through"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «TWIN TREES» (woh_roku:40). Opciones: pass through · go around.
msgctxt "woh_roku:43"
msgid "go around"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «TWIN TREES» (woh_roku:40).
msgctxt "woh_roku:44"
msgid ""
"You pass through, and it seems as though nothing happened. But you keep your eye out, and you swear, you keep noticing things that don't line up.\n"
"\n"
"Are the trees shifting? Or is the forest around them?\n"
"(+1 PERCEPTION)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «TWIN TREES» (woh_roku:40).
msgctxt "woh_roku:45"
msgid ""
"You pass through into the other woods and carry on. Then a fear settles into you that you might have made a mistake. That these are the wrong woods. And suddenly, nothing looks right anymore.\n"
"(+CURSE)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «TWIN TREES» (woh_roku:40).
msgctxt "woh_roku:46"
msgid ""
"When you look back, things appear normal again. The forest lines up with itself. This place is getting to you.\n"
"(-2 REASON)"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:47"
msgid "JUNPEI AND I"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «JUNPEI AND I» (woh_roku:47).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:48"
msgid ""
"You notice JUNPEI leafing through his notes as the three of you navigate the woods. You can't help yourself from looking over his shoulder.\n"
"\n"
"When he notices you, he sheepishly tucks the book against his chest. <<Oh, Makoto... Uh, this isn't related to the project.>>"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «JUNPEI AND I» (woh_roku:47). Opciones: <<Go ahead.>> · ask about notes.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:49"
msgid "<<Go ahead.>>"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «JUNPEI AND I» (woh_roku:47). Opciones: <<Go ahead.>> · ask about notes.
msgctxt "woh_roku:50"
msgid "ask about notes"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «JUNPEI AND I» (woh_roku:47).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:51"
msgid ""
"<<... Right. Thanks.>>\n"
"\n"
"He sighs and continues reading. You've known each other for a while, and he's known JUNPEI even longer, but JUNPEI still keeps his guard up about his hobbies. Sometimes it's good to remember you're not out to get one another.\n"
"(+STATUS)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «JUNPEI AND I» (woh_roku:47).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:52"
msgid ""
"As you express your curiosity, he perks up. <<Really? I didn't want to get on your nerves with more creepy stuff. I was just thinking about...>>\n"
"\n"
"He begins to explain a sacrificial healing rite local to the region. It's morbid, but his mellow tone and excited smile keep it from bothering you too badly.\n"
"(+SPELL)"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:53"
msgid "HITOMI AND I"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «HITOMI AND I» (woh_roku:53).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:54"
msgid ""
"Three sets of trudging footfalls are the only distraction you have from the tension out here.\n"
"A hand takes your shoulder, and you yelp. You turn to see HITOMI frowning, arm around you.\n"
"\n"
"<<Whoa.>> She blinks. <<I wasn't even trying to mess with you that time.>>"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «HITOMI AND I» (woh_roku:53). Opciones: <<Sorry.>> · <<I'm just nervous.>>.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:55"
msgid "<<Sorry.>>"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «HITOMI AND I» (woh_roku:53). Opciones: <<Sorry.>> · <<I'm just nervous.>>.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:56"
msgid "<<I'm just nervous.>>"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «HITOMI AND I» (woh_roku:53).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:57"
msgid ""
"<<Nothing to apologize for, man.>> She squeezes your shoulder. <<But you should really relax, you know? Panicking never helped anybody.>>\n"
"\n"
"You nod and try to calm your breathing. It'll be easier to focus if you stay calm. Clearly, HITOMI is pretty good at that...\n"
"(+STATUS)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «HITOMI AND I» (woh_roku:53).
#. Diálogo de HITOMI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:58"
msgid ""
"<<Yeah, this place is pretty freaky... Hey! I know what'll help.>>\n"
"HITOMI fishes around in her jacket, then presses something into your hands.\n"
"\n"
"<<And if that's not enough, don't forget I'm here too. I'll rough up some ghosts or whatever if you buy me a root beer tomorrow. Deal?>>\n"
"(+ITEM)"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:59"
msgid "PHOTOS SHACK"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «PHOTOS SHACK» (woh_roku:59).
msgctxt "woh_roku:60"
msgid "In the middle of a sparse clearing, a lone, jagged structure rises from the darkness. You near it tenuously, panning your viewfinder over the dilapidated wooden shack."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «PHOTOS SHACK» (woh_roku:59).
msgctxt "woh_roku:61"
msgid "As you step inside, the light catches on the pale borders of myriad photographs, pinned up across every inch of the interior. The wood is rotted, but the photos seem fairly recent, fresh. Each one has a name scratched onto it."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «PHOTOS SHACK» (woh_roku:59).
#. Diálogo de HITOMI, JUNPEI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:62"
msgid ""
"<<Freaky,>> HITOMI mumbles from over your shoulder.\n"
"\n"
"<<Don't some of them look familiar?>> JUNPEI asks. <<Maybe I'm imagining it, but I feel like I've seen them on the news or something.>>"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «PHOTOS SHACK» (woh_roku:59).
msgctxt "woh_roku:63"
msgid "You begin to step back, eager to leave, but you bump your heel against something hard. You look down to find..."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «PHOTOS SHACK» (woh_roku:59).
msgctxt "woh_roku:64"
msgid "Something heavy"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «PHOTOS SHACK» (woh_roku:59).
msgctxt "woh_roku:65"
msgid "Something sharp"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «PHOTOS SHACK» (woh_roku:59).
msgctxt "woh_roku:66"
msgid "Something obtuse"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «PHOTOS SHACK» (woh_roku:59).
msgctxt "woh_roku:67"
msgid ""
"You kneel down to find an industrial-looking flashlight. You wipe the mud off the lens and flick the switch. With a crackling sound, the old lamp flickers to life.\n"
"(+ITEM)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «PHOTOS SHACK» (woh_roku:59).
msgctxt "woh_roku:68"
msgid ""
"A glint catches along the edge of a dirty knife. As you wipe it off, the blade appears stained.\n"
"\n"
"Something in your gut tells you to keep it.\n"
"(+ITEM)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «PHOTOS SHACK» (woh_roku:59).
msgctxt "woh_roku:69"
msgid ""
"As you tear the odd shape from the dirt, you realize you're holding a flare gun. It looks to be loaded. You feel unnerved carrying it, but it could be helpful if you get lost.\n"
"(+ITEM)"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:70"
msgid "RITUAL CIRCLE"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «RITUAL CIRCLE» (woh_roku:70).
msgctxt "woh_roku:71"
msgid "The trees thin out in this direction. Some part of you hoped it might be the edge of the forest, but instead, you find yourself nearing a wide clearing. Rocks twice your height rise from the grass, like the teeth of some ancient predator."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «RITUAL CIRCLE» (woh_roku:70).
msgctxt "woh_roku:72"
msgid "HITOMI gasps, her hands clamping over her mouth. You don't understand why until your eyes adjust to the dark and you see it. White chalk trails among the rocks, arcane symbols, the plants dried out and burnt, the faded stench of decay."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «RITUAL CIRCLE» (woh_roku:70).
#. Diálogo de JUNPEI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:73"
msgid ""
"JUNPEI looks on in awe. <<What is this doing out here? That's a serious ritual circle...>>\n"
"\n"
"<<What? H-hey, don't joke around about this stuff.>> JUNPEI's voice falters in a way you haven't ever heard before. \n"
"\n"
"<<I'm not. As far as I can tell, it's genuine.>>"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «RITUAL CIRCLE» (woh_roku:70).
#. Diálogo de JUNPEI, HITOMI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:74"
msgid ""
"You look between your friends. They look back at you. The cold air stings.\n"
"\n"
"HITOMI speaks, monotone. <<We'll document this. And then we're going home.>>\n"
"\n"
"<<Yeah,>> JUNPEI says. <<This is the only footage we need. Yeah. To hell with this place already.>>"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «RITUAL CIRCLE» (woh_roku:70).
msgctxt "woh_roku:75"
msgid ""
"Looking out into the clearing feels like staring over the edge of a bottomless, black pit. You can feel your heartbeat.\n"
"\n"
"Even with the night mode on, it's too far and too dark for the camcorder to capture the ritual circle. You'll need to get closer if you want to get any good footage."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_roku:76"
msgid "APPROACH"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_roku:77"
msgid "NOT YET"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_roku:78"
msgid "JUNPEI"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_roku:79"
msgid "reduce all damage taken by 1"
msgstr ""

#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:80"
msgid "<<This will look great>>"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_roku:81"
msgid "[otaku]"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_roku:82"
msgid "HITOMI"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_roku:83"
msgid "increase the speed of all offensive actions by 15%"
msgstr ""

#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:84"
msgid "<<let's get it over with>>"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_roku:85"
msgid "[slacker]"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:86"
msgid "NO GOING BACK"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «NO GOING BACK» (woh_roku:86).
msgctxt "woh_roku:87"
msgid ""
"You steel your nerves and step out from the treeline, feeling acutely vulnerable. JUNPEI and HITOMI follow a few steps behind you.\n"
"\n"
"Just this, and then you can go home, you tell yourself."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «NO GOING BACK» (woh_roku:86).
msgctxt "woh_roku:88"
msgid ""
"You walk around the circle, tracing the chalk sigils with your viewfinder. You weave through the clearing, around the rocks, into a patch of tall grass.\n"
"\n"
"Something gives way below your foot, and your heart stops."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «NO GOING BACK» (woh_roku:86).
msgctxt "woh_roku:89"
msgid "The world grinds into slow motion as you realize your mistake. You're aware of every detail, but incapable of stopping it. The snap of releasing springs, the screech of steel, the rush of air behind the closing jaws."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «NO GOING BACK» (woh_roku:86).
msgctxt "woh_roku:90"
msgid "For a fleeting instant, your leg goes numb. Then it's agony, bright, searing red pain streaking up out of the darkness, drowning out every other nerve, your mind incapable of any thoughts beyond the raw urge to scream."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «NO GOING BACK» (woh_roku:86).
msgctxt "woh_roku:91"
msgid ""
"Your senses fall away as you crumple to the dirt. You only distantly hear your own voice, see your friends rush to your side.\n"
"\n"
"You only regain awareness when you feel the bear trap wrenched off of your leg."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «NO GOING BACK» (woh_roku:86).
msgctxt "woh_roku:92"
msgid "The trap falls away with a clatter. You lay reeling. There's a cloying pain as the blood flows from the wound. JUNPEI is panicking, and HITOMI is apologizing. Somebody holds your hand."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «NO GOING BACK» (woh_roku:86).
msgctxt "woh_roku:93"
msgid "JUNPEI grabs your other pant leg. You hear the rip of fabric, and he gets to work wrapping the injury. HITOMI snaps a heavy branch for him, and he sets a makeshift splint. The pain lingers, but your heartbeat begins to calm."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «NO GOING BACK» (woh_roku:86).
#. Diálogo de HITOMI, JUNPEI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:94"
msgid ""
"JUNPEI leans over you. You see the fear in his eyes. <<This is insane. We need to go get help-->>\n"
"\n"
"<<No!>> HITOMI shouts, startling both of you. <<There's no way in hell we're leaving MAKOTO out here alone!>>"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «NO GOING BACK» (woh_roku:86).
#. Diálogo de HITOMI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:95"
msgid ""
"He hesitates. <<Then you go. I can fend for myself here with MAKOTO.>>\n"
"HITOMI grimaces.\n"
"\n"
"<<What if whoever set that thing comes back? Can you protect yourselves then?>>\n"
"Silence falls as you all realize the full weight of the situation..."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «NO GOING BACK» (woh_roku:86).
msgctxt "woh_roku:96"
msgid "send away JUNPEI"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «NO GOING BACK» (woh_roku:86).
msgctxt "woh_roku:97"
msgid "send away HITOMI"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «NO GOING BACK» (woh_roku:86).
msgctxt "woh_roku:98"
msgid "send away both"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «NO GOING BACK» (woh_roku:86).
#. Diálogo de JUNPEI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:99"
msgid ""
"<<... Stay here, HITOMI.>>\n"
"\n"
"She moves immediately to your side, hand on your shoulder. <<Whatever you say. I'm here.>>\n"
"\n"
"JUNPEI looks as if he's about to say something, but holds it back. He just nods solemnly. <<Then I'll go. Stay right here, I won't take long.>>"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «NO GOING BACK» (woh_roku:86).
#. Diálogo de HITOMI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:100"
msgid ""
"She stares out into the dark, her expression unreadable.\n"
"\n"
"<<He's still not back yet. He should be back by now. Why isn't he...>>\n"
"\n"
"HITOMI abruptly gets up. Something feels off about her. You're not sure what.\n"
"<<We've got to look for him. Can you walk?>>"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «NO GOING BACK» (woh_roku:86).
#. Diálogo de HITOMI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:101"
msgid ""
"<<JUNPEI... I trust you.>>\n"
"\n"
"He gives you a surprised look. Then, he pushes his glasses up onto his face, taking a slow breath. <<Alright. Then I'll stay.>>\n"
"\n"
"HITOMI looks between the two of you, uncertain. Her expression softens. <<Okay. You see anything, run the hell away. Got it?>>"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «NO GOING BACK» (woh_roku:86).
msgctxt "woh_roku:102"
msgid ""
"You nod, and she takes off straight into the trees. JUNPEI sits down to accompany you.\n"
"\n"
"Your friend tries to make some small talk to break up the silence as you wait, but he struggles to come up with much. The time slips past, an hour, maybe more. HITOMI hasn't come back yet."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «NO GOING BACK» (woh_roku:86).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:103"
msgid ""
"JUNPEI's small talk has devolved into muttering under his breath. You can't make out his words.\n"
"\n"
"Suddenly, as if possessed, he gets to his feet.\n"
"\n"
"<<It's not safe here. It's not safe here, MAKOTO. We need to go. Okay?>>"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «NO GOING BACK» (woh_roku:86).
#. Diálogo de HITOMI, JUNPEI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:104"
msgid ""
"<<... I'll be fine alone.>>\n"
"\n"
"They both turn to you. <<Are you crazy?>> HITOMI says in disbelief. JUNPEI agrees, <<She's right, we can't just...>>"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «NO GOING BACK» (woh_roku:86).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:105"
msgid ""
"You stare back, intense. You refuse to let either of them go out alone. Your friends, stunned, lose their nerve.\n"
"\n"
"<<If you're certain, then... alright. We'll be back as soon as we can.>>\n"
"\n"
"They reluctantly set out into the forest together."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «NO GOING BACK» (woh_roku:86).
msgctxt "woh_roku:106"
msgid ""
"You lay there for some time.\n"
"Then, some time longer. \n"
" There are no signs of anyone.\n"
"\n"
"The pain has slowly begun to subside. You force yourself upright. You manage to get your legs beneath you and limp out of the clearing."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «NO GOING BACK» (woh_roku:86).
msgctxt "woh_roku:107"
msgid "The forests outside SHIOKAWA have always had a strange reputation."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_roku:108"
msgid "MYSTERY TITLE>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_roku:109"
msgid "find your way out of the forest"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_roku:110"
msgid "BAD DECISIONS A"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_roku:111"
msgid "BAD DECISIONS B"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:112"
msgid "BAD DECISIONS C"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «BAD DECISIONS C» (woh_roku:112).
msgctxt "woh_roku:113"
msgid ""
"He walks away, disappearing into the forest, and HITOMI keeps silent watch.\n"
"\n"
" You're not sure how long the two of you wait there. An hour, maybe even two. \n"
"\n"
"Your pain lessens, but HITOMI only grows more tense, to the point of visibly shaking."
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «BAD DECISIONS C» (woh_roku:112). Opciones: ABANDONED BUNKER.
msgctxt "woh_roku:114"
msgid "ABANDONED BUNKER"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «BAD DECISIONS C» (woh_roku:112).
msgctxt "woh_roku:115"
msgid "You have to catch yourself not to fall into the yawning hole in the dirt. As your eyes adjust, you realize you're staring into the entrance of a bunker. Heavy, stifling air fills your lungs as you stagger down the concrete steps."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «BAD DECISIONS C» (woh_roku:112).
msgctxt "woh_roku:116"
msgid "Murky water pools along the interior of the bunker, at least a foot deep. The place looks as if it were utterly forgotten after the war, and nature is beginning to reclaim it with tendrils of moss."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «BAD DECISIONS C» (woh_roku:112).
msgctxt "woh_roku:117"
msgid "You're not eager to venture any further. You can't tell what's in the water, or whether your injury might get infected if you wade through. But if you risk it, there's likely to be some useful supplies..."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «BAD DECISIONS C» (woh_roku:112).
msgctxt "woh_roku:118"
msgid "search barracks"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «BAD DECISIONS C» (woh_roku:112).
msgctxt "woh_roku:119"
msgid "search armory"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «BAD DECISIONS C» (woh_roku:112).
msgctxt "woh_roku:120"
msgid "turn back"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «BAD DECISIONS C» (woh_roku:112).
msgctxt "woh_roku:121"
msgid ""
"Wading deep through waterlogged storage, your eye is caught by a satchel labeled with a cross. While the medicine has long since expired, the rest of the first aid kit is, miraculously, intact.\n"
"(+ITEM / +STATUS)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «BAD DECISIONS C» (woh_roku:112).
msgctxt "woh_roku:122"
msgid ""
"Years of exposure to the elements have rusted the rifles and rotted the ammunition. Only a handful of bullets remain in usable condition.\n"
"(+ITEM / +STATUS)"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:123"
msgid "TEETH ALTAR"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «TEETH ALTAR» (woh_roku:123).
msgctxt "woh_roku:124"
msgid "In the darkness, you find yourself stumbling as you nearly trip over something. Looking down, you find a small rock surrounded by large teeth planted in the dirt, criss-crossed with pale chalk sigils."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «TEETH ALTAR» (woh_roku:123).
msgctxt "woh_roku:125"
msgid ""
"It bears an uncomfortably close resemblance to a miniature version of the ritual circle from earlier.\n"
"\n"
"Atop the rock is a stained notebook. Nearby, as you look around, you notice a pair of bolt cutters embedded in the ground."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «TEETH ALTAR» (woh_roku:123).
msgctxt "woh_roku:126"
msgid "take the bolt cutter and the notebook"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «TEETH ALTAR» (woh_roku:123).
msgctxt "woh_roku:127"
msgid "leave"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:128"
msgid "WITCH TWINS"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «WITCH TWINS» (woh_roku:128).
msgctxt "woh_roku:129"
msgid ""
"Above you, you see red.\n"
"\n"
"A snarl of red ropes, strangling the trees.\n"
"\n"
"They shimmer in the wind, swaying, and then shaking, growing more violent by the second.\n"
"\n"
"Something is approaching..."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «WITCH TWINS» (woh_roku:128).
msgctxt "woh_roku:130"
msgid "The corrupting effect of the OLD GODS has awakened the ancient witches."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «WITCH TWINS» (woh_roku:128).
msgctxt "woh_roku:131"
msgid "Red ropes begin to bind your legs!"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «WITCH TWINS» (woh_roku:128).
msgctxt "woh_roku:132"
msgid "You continue to bleed out!"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «WITCH TWINS» (woh_roku:128).
msgctxt "woh_roku:133"
msgid "You feel weaker!"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:134"
msgid "THE HOUSE"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «THE HOUSE» (woh_roku:134).
msgctxt "woh_roku:135"
msgid ""
"Abruptly, the forest is gored through by a massive wooden structure. Loosely, it resembles a traditional style house, but piled up on itself, scraping against the trees until it disappears up into their branches.\n"
"\n"
" It's an ungodly and strange thing to see after what feels like miles of indistinct forest."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «THE HOUSE» (woh_roku:134).
msgctxt "woh_roku:136"
msgid ""
"Despite what must be decades of rot, with not even a worn path in the dirt to suggest occupancy, it remains standing, and it towers over you.\n"
"\n"
"This house shouldn't be here. Neither should you.\n"
"\n"
"The front door is chained shut. Something is waiting for you inside."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «THE HOUSE» (woh_roku:134).
msgctxt "woh_roku:137"
msgid "turn back"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «THE HOUSE» (woh_roku:134).
msgctxt "woh_roku:138"
msgid "use the BOLT CUTTER, and enter"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «THE HOUSE» (woh_roku:134).
msgctxt "woh_roku:139"
msgid ""
"The chain snaps, clattering onto the porch's rotten floorboards.\n"
"\n"
"You give in to fate and step through..."
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:140"
msgid "WITCH TWINS' LAIR"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «WITCH TWINS' LAIR» (woh_roku:140).
msgctxt "woh_roku:141"
msgid "You march into the darkness ahead. Suddenly, your foot meets air where you expected dirt, and you slip. You tumble down the gully, sharp pain jolting through your leg with each impact, until you finally roll to a stop."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «WITCH TWINS' LAIR» (woh_roku:140).
msgctxt "woh_roku:142"
msgid "Before you is a yawning crater, paved with withered grass. The trees line the ridge but don't dare descend into it. Between them are woven countless red ropes, unnaturally pristine. The place is smothered in an anxious silence, but for now, it seems safe."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «WITCH TWINS' LAIR» (woh_roku:140).
msgctxt "woh_roku:143"
msgid ""
"Among the tangle of crimson threads, you spot two small shapes. The tiny humanoid figures look as though they've been hanged.\n"
"\n"
"Unfortunately, you think you may recognize them."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «WITCH TWINS' LAIR» (woh_roku:140).
msgctxt "woh_roku:144"
msgid "take the dolls and continue"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_roku:145"
msgid "TWINS' EFFIGIES"
msgstr ""

#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:146"
msgid "<<uncanny resemblance>>"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_roku:147"
msgid "Occult dolls used to summon a doppelganger puppet of their respective likenesses."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "woh_roku:148"
msgid "Your fingertips feel numb when you hold these dolls..."
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:149"
msgid "JUNPEI'S CORPSE"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «JUNPEI'S CORPSE» (woh_roku:149).
msgctxt "woh_roku:150"
msgid "HITOMI gasps as you step through the brush. Before you, something pale, red, spilled all over, splayed out across the forest floor. The shape is malformed and difficult to even make sense of in the darkness. You can't tell where the foliage stops and the viscera starts."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «JUNPEI'S CORPSE» (woh_roku:149).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:151"
msgid ""
"\n"
"\n"
"<<Oh, god...>>\n"
"\n"
"As you struggle to make sense of the scene, a glint catches your eye. You pluck it from the ground. In your hands lies his notebook.\n"
"\n"
"This is all that's left of JUNPEI.\n"
"(+ITEM / -3 ALL)"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:152"
msgid "WITCH'S HOUSE"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «WITCH'S HOUSE» (woh_roku:152).
msgctxt "woh_roku:153"
msgid ""
"The house is... empty.\n"
"\n"
"No traps, no voices, just dust and the faint smell of damp earth.\n"
"You descend into the basement, each step heavy with exhaustion."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «WITCH'S HOUSE» (woh_roku:152).
msgctxt "woh_roku:154"
msgid ""
"You set the camera down beside the gaping hole in the floor. You're too weak to be carrying it anymore.\n"
"\n"
"You tell yourself you'll rest only for a moment, just until the pain in your leg becomes manageable again, just until you stop shaking."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «WITCH'S HOUSE» (woh_roku:152).
msgctxt "woh_roku:155"
msgid ""
"The silence stretches.\n"
"\n"
"When you finally climb up back the stairs, you don't look back. The camera keeps recording, pointed at the hole."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «WITCH'S HOUSE» (woh_roku:152).
msgctxt "woh_roku:156"
msgid ""
"Maybe your friends have already found help.\n"
"\n"
"Maybe they're still out there, following you deeper into the woods."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «WITCH'S HOUSE» (woh_roku:152).
msgctxt "woh_roku:157"
msgid "The woods are quiet now, too quiet."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «WITCH'S HOUSE» (woh_roku:152).
msgctxt "woh_roku:158"
msgid "You call out, but no one answers."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «WITCH'S HOUSE» (woh_roku:152).
msgctxt "woh_roku:159"
msgid "You don't remember when your leg stopped hurting."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «WITCH'S HOUSE» (woh_roku:152).
msgctxt "woh_roku:160"
msgid "You've been walking for hours… maybe days."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «WITCH'S HOUSE» (woh_roku:152).
msgctxt "woh_roku:161"
msgid "The rescue team must be nearby."
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:162"
msgid "JUNPEI AND I"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «JUNPEI AND I» (woh_roku:162).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:163"
msgid ""
"You notice JUNPEI leafing through his notes as the three of you navigate the woods. You can't help yourself from looking over his shoulder.\n"
"\n"
"When he notices you, he sheepishly tucks the book against his chest. <<Oh, Makoto... Uh, this isn't related to the project.>>"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «JUNPEI AND I» (woh_roku:162). Opciones: <<Go ahead.>> · ask about notes.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:164"
msgid "<<Go ahead.>>"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «JUNPEI AND I» (woh_roku:162). Opciones: <<Go ahead.>> · ask about notes.
msgctxt "woh_roku:165"
msgid "ask about notes"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «JUNPEI AND I» (woh_roku:162).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:166"
msgid ""
"<<... Right. Thanks.>>\n"
"\n"
"He sighs and continues reading. You've known each other for a while, and he's known HITOMI even longer, but JUNPEI still keeps his guard up about his hobbies. Sometimes it's good to remember you're not out to get one another.\n"
"(+PERK)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «JUNPEI AND I» (woh_roku:162).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:167"
msgid ""
"As you express your curiosity, he perks up. <<Really? I didn't want to get on your nerves with more creepy stuff. I was just thinking about...>>\n"
"\n"
"He begins to explain a sacrificial healing rite local to the region. It's morbid, but his mellow tone and excited smile keep it from bothering you too badly.\n"
"(+SPELL)"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:168"
msgid "HITOMI AND I"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «HITOMI AND I» (woh_roku:168).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:169"
msgid ""
"Three sets of trudging footfalls are the only distraction you have from the tension out here.\n"
"A hand takes your shoulder, and you yelp. You turn to see HITOMI frowning, arm around you.\n"
"\n"
"<<Whoa.>> She blinks. <<I wasn't even trying to mess with you that time.>>"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «HITOMI AND I» (woh_roku:168). Opciones: <<Sorry.>> · << I'm just nervous.>>.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:170"
msgid "<<Sorry.>>"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «HITOMI AND I» (woh_roku:168). Opciones: <<Sorry.>> · << I'm just nervous.>>.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:171"
msgid "<< I'm just nervous.>>"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «HITOMI AND I» (woh_roku:168).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:172"
msgid ""
"<<Nothing to apologize for, man.>> She squeezes your shoulder. <<But you should really relax, you know? Panicking never helped anybody. >>\n"
"\n"
"You nod and try to calm your breathing. It'll be easier to focus if you stay calm. Clearly, HITOMI is pretty good at that...\n"
"(+PERK)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «HITOMI AND I» (woh_roku:168).
#. Diálogo de HITOMI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:173"
msgid ""
"<<Yeah, this place is pretty freaky... Hey! I know what'll help.>>\n"
"HITOMI fishes around in her jacket, then presses something into your hands.\n"
"\n"
"<<And if that's not enough, don't forget I'm here too. I'll rough up some ghosts or whatever if you buy me a root beer tomorrow. Deal?>>\n"
"(+ITEM)"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:174"
msgid "JUNPEI"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «JUNPEI» (woh_roku:174).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:175"
msgid ""
"You trudge on through the endless forest. JUNPEI isn't far behind you. With each step, you hear his breathing grow more ragged. Then there's a choked voice. Then tears. \n"
"\n"
"<<You should've left me behind. This... this is all my fault...>>"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «JUNPEI» (woh_roku:174). Opciones: <<No, it isn't.>> · <<...>> · embrace him.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:176"
msgid "<<No, it isn't.>>"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «JUNPEI» (woh_roku:174). Opciones: <<No, it isn't.>> · <<...>> · embrace him.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:177"
msgid "<<...>>"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «JUNPEI» (woh_roku:174). Opciones: <<No, it isn't.>> · <<...>> · embrace him.
msgctxt "woh_roku:178"
msgid "embrace him"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «JUNPEI» (woh_roku:174).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:179"
msgid ""
"<<Don't lie to me!>> he snaps. <<I know I'm the only reason we're out here, me and my stupid hobby!>>\n"
"\n"
"Your voice is too weak to argue with him. But it doesn't matter whose fault it is. You're here now, and you need to get them home. No matter what.\n"
"(+PERK)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «JUNPEI» (woh_roku:174).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:180"
msgid ""
"<<I should just die. Just get it over with. It's hopeless.>>\n"
"\n"
"Your head falls. You can't let him do that. You've always known that you would give up your life in exchange for his. And you will, if you have to.\n"
"(+PERK)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «JUNPEI» (woh_roku:174).
msgctxt "woh_roku:181"
msgid ""
"You hold on to him as though he could be ripped away from you at any moment. His face falls into your shoulder, and he sobs. You do your best to comfort him. Your friends have been strong for you so many times.\n"
"\n"
"Now it's your turn.\n"
"(+50 EXPERIENCE)"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:182"
msgid "HITOMI"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «HITOMI» (woh_roku:182).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:183"
msgid "Pitch darkness swallows the treeline beyond a few feet away. The leaves crunch beneath your feet as you guide HITOMI along. She mutters to herself. Then, a little louder, she asks, <<You know how we first met?>>"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «HITOMI» (woh_roku:182). Opciones: <<Why do you ask?>> · <<I remember.>> · <<...>>.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:184"
msgid "<<Why do you ask?>>"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «HITOMI» (woh_roku:182). Opciones: <<Why do you ask?>> · <<I remember.>> · <<...>>.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:185"
msgid "<<I remember.>>"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «HITOMI» (woh_roku:182). Opciones: <<Why do you ask?>> · <<I remember.>> · <<...>>.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:186"
msgid "<<...>>"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «HITOMI» (woh_roku:182).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:187"
msgid ""
"<<I don't want to die.>> Her voice is shallow and flat. << Don't leave me. I don't want to go.>>\n"
"\n"
"Her numb fingers lace into yours as you silently take her hand. You'll protect her. Somehow, you'll protect her.\n"
"(+PERK)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «HITOMI» (woh_roku:182).
msgctxt "woh_roku:188"
msgid ""
"You tell her about visiting the record store, looking for music to use in your film projects. She worked there part-time, and you gradually grew closer. Dwelling on the memory together helps you hold on to yourselves just a little longer.\n"
"(+50 EXPERIENCE)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «HITOMI» (woh_roku:182).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:189"
msgid ""
"<<I can't remember. It's gone. Please, please tell me you remember.>>\n"
"\n"
"She looks to you, pleading, but you can't help. The memory has decayed. Horror and relief settle in your stomach like oil and water as you understand that you'll never leave this place.\n"
"(+PERK)"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:190"
msgid "THE TALL MAN"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «THE TALL MAN» (woh_roku:190).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:191"
msgid ""
"It isn't until the man clears his throat that you notice him, gaunt and deathly still, easily mistaken for another tree in the dark. He watches you coldly.\n"
"\n"
"<<Tell me, kid,>> the man asks in an uneven drone, <<do you think you'll survive the night?>>"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «THE TALL MAN» (woh_roku:190). Opciones: <<Yes.>> · <<No.>> · <<...>>.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:192"
msgid "<<Yes.>>"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «THE TALL MAN» (woh_roku:190). Opciones: <<Yes.>> · <<No.>> · <<...>>.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:193"
msgid "<<No.>>"
msgstr ""

#. Opción de «THE TALL MAN» (woh_roku:190). Opciones: <<Yes.>> · <<No.>> · <<...>>.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:194"
msgid "<<...>>"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «THE TALL MAN» (woh_roku:190).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:195"
msgid ""
"His eyes bore into yours. Then he shrugs. <<Who am I to tell you otherwise?>> He walks off with a dismissive wave of his hand.\n"
"\n"
"<<Go on, then. Do your best to keep living.>>\n"
"(+PERK)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «THE TALL MAN» (woh_roku:190).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:196"
msgid ""
"He steps closer, a cold hand taking your shoulder. << You're right. For you, it's the end of the line. Your friends, though...>>\n"
"\n"
"With a sneer, he steps past you, and disappears into the forest.\n"
"\n"
"<<Well, do what you can.>>\n"
"(+PERK)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «THE TALL MAN» (woh_roku:190).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:197"
msgid ""
"You tremble before the man, voice caught in your throat. He groans. <<What a mess. All because those idiots won't leave well enough alone.>> \n"
"\n"
"He tosses something to you - out of pity, maybe - and when you look up from catching it, he's gone.\n"
"(+ITEM)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «THE TALL MAN» (woh_roku:190).
msgctxt "woh_roku:198"
msgid "You've rested a bit. (+1 REASON)"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «THE TALL MAN» (woh_roku:190).
msgctxt "woh_roku:199"
msgid "You've rested a bit. (+1 STAMINA)"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:200"
msgid "THE END OF THE ROAD"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «THE END OF THE ROAD» (woh_roku:200).
msgctxt "woh_roku:201"
msgid ""
"You enter the house, clutching the doll effigies of your two friends.\n"
"\n"
"The pain in your leg is mostly gone, replaced by a dull throbbing sensation creeping higher with each step.\n"
"\n"
"You're not sure whether that's a good sign or if you've already lost too much blood."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «THE END OF THE ROAD» (woh_roku:200).
msgctxt "woh_roku:202"
msgid ""
"The air inside the house is still and heavy with damp earth.\n"
"\n"
"An unseen force is guiding you towards the small room in the back, where you find JUNPEI and HITOMI. They are exhausted and terrified but alive."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «THE END OF THE ROAD» (woh_roku:200).
msgctxt "woh_roku:203"
msgid ""
"You place the two dolls on the ground to untie your friend when something unexpected happens.\n"
"\n"
"The threads begin to unravel on their own, growing and stitching flesh from cloth…"
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «THE END OF THE ROAD» (woh_roku:200).
msgctxt "woh_roku:204"
msgid ""
"Two figures rise, wrong but convincing enough.\n"
"\n"
"JUNPEI's laugh is too loud, and HITOMI's nose is slightly crooked. You've created LIVING EFFIGIES."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «THE END OF THE ROAD» (woh_roku:200).
msgctxt "woh_roku:205"
msgid ""
"Hearing voices approaching the house, you make a quick decision.\n"
"\n"
"You will only slow your friends down.\n"
"\n"
"You push the real JUNPEI and HITOMI toward the back door. The forest swallows them quickly. HITOMI looks back at you one last time before disappearing."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «THE END OF THE ROAD» (woh_roku:200).
msgctxt "woh_roku:206"
msgid ""
"Hands seize you from behind.\n"
"\n"
"You don't struggle.\n"
"\n"
"The cult drags you and two living dolls towards the basement. You're forced to your knees in front of a massive hole in the floor. Below, something stirs, pleased."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «THE END OF THE ROAD» (woh_roku:200).
msgctxt "woh_roku:207"
msgid "The last thing you hear is the sound of stitching coming undone..."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «THE END OF THE ROAD» (woh_roku:200).
msgctxt "woh_roku:208"
msgid "JUNPEI and HITOMI emerged out of the forest the next morning, miles from where the trees first closed around them. They were starved, shaking, and unable to agree on how long they had been lost. They've never told anyone about the house."
msgstr ""

#. Parte de «THE END OF THE ROAD» (woh_roku:200).
msgctxt "woh_roku:209"
msgid ""
"The third student's body was never found. The documentary was never finished. Warped footage and half-recorded whispers are the only proof someone was there…\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"and that they were not meant ever to leave.\n"
"[FOREST OF FEAR / TAPES OF TRAGEDY: ENDING A]"
msgstr ""

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:210"
msgid "FOREST OF FEAR / TAPES OF TRAGEDY"
msgstr ""

#. Descripción de «FOREST OF FEAR / TAPES OF TRAGEDY» (woh_roku:210).
msgctxt "woh_roku:211"
msgid ""
"In March 1985, three students from the AV club set out to film a documentary about the forest’s oldest legend: the witch said to have been buried alive beneath her own house. It was meant to be a quick shoot, an eerie little project they could wrap up before sunset.\n"
"\n"
"They never returned and remain missing to this day."
msgstr ""

